+- Race data (4.0.1, `remote_race.c`): a race opens `Course/<name>/` (`Gu_Menu` behind the menus). One object of class main+0x125ada8 holds a `sead::PtrArray` of the racers at +0x60 / +0x68, player 1 first; a racer (class main+0x12cac28) has its index at +0x38, its 0-based place at +0x40, 0-based lap at +0x44 and coins at +0x50. Found with `DM_CTL scan` (`hle_scan.c`: `scan i32 1 10`, `scan rec` with a `shot` after each, `scan match` against the shots; `scan ptr64` for the owners) in two races of a 50cc cup; the objects lived across the cup's races. A kart model (class main+0x125a288, one per racer, made in racer order in each kart's own heap; it names `Driver/<name>.bfres`, `Kart/Body/…`, `Kart/Tire/…`, `Kart/Wing/…`) has the character at +0x8 (its colour at +0xc), body +0x14, glider +0x18, tires +0x20; the ids follow the menus' part lists (`Mario` … `Pauline`, `K_Std` …, `T_Std` …, `G_Std` …, built on the heap as name and label tables), and `Driver/DrvChr0N` is character 43 + N (Birdo 44 … Pauline 51). The item box (class main+0x127e110, one object while one player races) has its two slots' states at +0x200 (3 holding, 2 roulette, 0 empty) and items at +0x210; item ids are the index of the u8 table at main+0xf21e7c (id → frame of the box's `ItemPtn` icon animation in `UI/cmn/race.sarc` `rc_L_ItemBox_00`: 0 banana, 1 green shell, 2 red shell, 3 mushroom, 15 coin checked on screen). The racers' own item slots were not found (not plain int32). `DM_CTL scan seq i32 <max stride> <ids…>` found the per-racer arrays from the line-up the results screen shows.
 
